From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wai Chung <hello@ternii.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] ggml: dense trit types TQ9_128 / TQ27_128 / TQ81_128
 (CPU)

Adds three block types for exact k-trit integer codes with one fp16 key
per 128 weights: weight = key * q, q in [-(N-1)/2, (N-1)/2], N = 9 / 27 / 81
levels (2 / 3 / 4 trits). Codes are packed 5 per 16 / 24 / 32-bit word in
mixed radix (3.375 / 5.000 / 6.625 bits per weight including the key).
CPU reference quantize / dequantize, vec_dot against Q8_0 activations,
GGUF type ids 44-46, llama ftypes, gguf-py constants, test-backend-ops.
